window.PET_DATA["knowledge/grammar-07-relative-clauses.json"] = {"id":"grammar-07","type":"grammar","title":"Relative Clauses","objective":"Use who, which, that, where and whose to add information about people, things and places.","sections":[{"heading":"Choosing the pronoun","body":"`who` (or that) for people: `the teacher who teaches us English`\n`which` (or that) for things: `the book which I borrowed`\n`where` for places: `the town where I was born`\n`whose` for possession: `the girl whose brother is famous`\n`that` works for people and things in defining clauses and is very common in spoken English.","bodyZh":"who 指人，which 指物，where 指地点，whose 表所属；在限定性定语从句中 that 人和物都可用，口语中很常见。","examples":[{"en":"I met a woman who speaks six languages.","zh":"我遇到一位会说六种语言的女士。"},{"en":"This is the cafe where we first met.","zh":"这就是我们初次见面的咖啡馆。"}],"tip":"In open cloze (Reading Part 6), relative pronouns are among the most common missing words."},{"heading":"Defining relative clauses","body":"A defining clause tells us exactly which person/thing we mean — no commas: `The man who lives next door is a pilot.`\nAt B1 you mostly need defining clauses. If the pronoun is the object of the clause, it can be omitted: `The film (that) I saw yesterday was great.`","bodyZh":"限定性定语从句说明具体指哪一个，不用逗号。当代词在从句中作宾语时可以省略。","examples":[{"en":"Students who arrive late miss the registration.","zh":"迟到的学生会错过签到。"},{"en":"The phone I bought last week is already broken!","zh":"我上周买的手机已经坏了！"}],"tip":"Notice the omitted pronoun pattern — PET Reading uses it constantly."},{"heading":"Prepositions in relative clauses","body":"Keep the preposition with its verb at the end of the clause: `the person I was talking to`, `the bus I'm waiting for`.\nFormal style puts it before the pronoun (`to whom`), but at B1 the end position is natural and correct.","bodyZh":"介词通常保留在从句末尾（the person I was talking to）；to whom 的正式写法了解即可。","examples":[{"en":"She's the friend who I went on holiday with.","zh":"她就是我和她一起去度假的那个朋友。"}],"tip":"Don't drop the preposition: the friend who I went on holiday (wrong)."}],"commonErrors":[{"wrong":"The man which lives next door...","right":"The man who lives next door...","why":"Use who/that for people, which for things."},{"wrong":"the town that I was born","right":"the town where I was born","why":"Places need where (or in which)."},{"wrong":"The girl which brother is famous","right":"The girl whose brother is famous","why":"whose shows possession."}],"summary":{"keyPoints":["who = people · which = things · where = places · whose = possession.","that can replace who/which in defining clauses.","Object pronouns can be omitted: the film (that) I saw.","Keep prepositions at the end: the friend I went with."],"mustKnow":["who lives","which I bought","where I was born","whose"]},"linkedPractice":["reading"],"reviewItems":[]};
